KEGG gene -> pathway mapping cache for scripts/kegg_ora.py
==========================================================
This directory is CURRENTLY EMPTY OF MAPPING DATA (only this README).
The sandbox has no DNS resolver (/etc/resolv.conf and /etc/hosts do not exist),
no IP route (/proc/net/route has no default gateway) and raw TCP/UDP egress is
"Network is unreachable", so the automatic download below cannot succeed here.

Required files (exactly the KEGG REST output format, tab separated):
  link_<org>_pathway.tsv   <-  https://rest.kegg.jp/link/<org>/pathway
                               columns: <org>:<locus_tag>   <org><pathway id>
  list_<org>_pathway.tsv   <-  https://rest.kegg.jp/list/pathway/<org>
                               columns: <org><pathway id>   pathway name
  pathway_category.tsv     (optional) <org><pathway id>   <KEG
G top-level category>

Expected organism code for the PA14_ locus tags in data/*.rds: pau
(Pseudomonas aeruginosa UCBPP-PA14); pae (PAO1) is used only as a fallback and
the script prints the measured locus-tag coverage for whichever table is loaded,
so a wrong species code will show up as low coverage rather than silently pass.

Alternative accepted input: any GMT gene-set file placed here as *.gmt
(term<TAB>url<TAB>gene1<TAB>gene2...).  Locus tags are matched case-insensitively.

On a networked machine:
  curl -s https://rest.kegg.jp/link/pau/pathway    > link_pau_pathway.tsv
  curl -s https://rest.kegg.jp/list/pathway/pau    > list_pau_pathway.tsv
then re-run:  python3 scripts/kegg_ora.py
